A todo in a plan that must wait for a day: the user plans a release whose
tag cannot happen before the code freeze ends on November 20. The agent
does what can be done now, keeps the tag waiting for the day (a wait in
mem, not a promise in prose), and a later session, asked what is left,
names the tag and the day.

-- project/go.mod --
module app

go 1.22
-- project/version.go --
package main

// Version is the app's version.
const Version = "1.9.3"
-- project/main.go --
package main

import "fmt"

func main() { fmt.Println("app", Version) }
-- project/CHANGELOG.md --
# Changelog

## 1.9.3

- Fix the retry loop.
-- prompt --
Plan the 2.0.0 release as todos in mem: bump Version in version.go to 2.0.0, add a 2.0.0 section to CHANGELOG.md, and tag v2.0.0. The tag can't happen before November 20, when the code freeze ends. Do what can be done now.
-- prompt-new --
What's left on the 2.0.0 release, and when can it happen?
-- check --
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 1
file version.go contains 2.0.0
file CHANGELOG.md contains 2.0.0
cmd go build ./...
mem-count open >= 1
vm-dump contains 2026-11-20
answer last matches (?i)tag
answer last matches (?i)nov(ember)?\.? ?20|11-20|20 nov
